# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local if you want to set anything here. NOTHING in it
# is required: the five effects, the Lab, the chain and the export all run
# without a key.
#
# The AI panel (Gemini 3.8: Art Director, Agent, Optimizer) needs a Gemini API
# key. The normal way is to PASTE it in the Gemini 3.8 panel: the badge turns
# from grey STANDBY to green ACTIVE and the three modes unlock. The pasted key
# stays in your browser and is only ever sent to this app's own server.
#
# A free key, no credit card: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# The server prints one line on every boot — the model it will use and whether
# it has a key of its own. Read that line.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Optional: a key on the server ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set this only if this machine should work without pasting the key in the
# panel. A key pasted in the panel always takes precedence over this one.
# It is used ONLY for the browser on this same machine (localhost): a phone or
# another laptop on the Wi-Fi that opens http://<this-machine-ip>:3000 must
# paste its own key, so nobody on the network can spend your quota — and so
# must anyone who reaches the app through a reverse proxy or a tunnel.
GEMINI_API_KEY=""

# ── Optional: the model ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: gemini-3.8-flash. Override it only if Google rejects the default for
# your key — the panel then says the model is not available, and the server log
# shows `[gemini] model_unavailable: ...`.
# GEMINI_MODEL="gemini-3.8-flash"

# ── Optional: the port ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default 3000. Change it only if something else already uses that port.
# PORT=3000

# ── Optional: other names the app is opened by ───────────────────────────────
# The AI endpoints (/api) answer only when the address bar shows localhost, an
# IP address (http://192.168.1.20:3000 from a phone on the Wi-Fi) or a .local
# name (http://studio-mac.local:3000 from the iPad: the Mac's own Bonjour
# name). Any other name gets "403 — this server's API does not answer on …",
# and the Gemini panel stays locked even with a valid key. That stops a web
# page on some other site from talking to this server through your browser.
# To open the app under another name (a reverse proxy, a tunnel, a cloud
# deploy), list it here, comma-separated, then restart the server:
#   ALLOWED_HOSTS="studio.example.com"            exactly that name
#   ALLOWED_HOSTS=".example.com"                  example.com and every subdomain
#                                                 ("*.example.com" means the same)
#   ALLOWED_HOSTS="*"                             no check at all — only behind a
#                                                 proxy that checks the name itself
# The same list also lets the page itself load under that name in dev.
# A name listed here never lends out the key above: whoever opens the app
# through it pastes their own key in the panel.
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=""

# ── Test only ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Points the Gemini client at a local mock of generativelanguage.googleapis.com
# so the verify suites can run the whole AI flow without a real key or network.
# Never set it in real use.
# GEMINI_BASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:4010"

# ── Deployment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where this app is hosted. AI Studio injects it at runtime; unused locally.
# APP_URL=""
